FACT 6
∇
∇R←I X
R←X
∇
∇R←X K Y
R←X
∇
∇R←X KI Y
R←Y
∇
∇NOTHERE
'M  MOCKINGBIRD. M X IS X X, A FUNCTION APPLIED TO ITSELF. THE'
'   FUNCTIONS HERE ARE NAMED BY A GLYPH, AND NO PRIMITIVE TAKES A'
'   GLYPH AS ITS ARGUMENT, SO THERE IS NO X X TO FORM.'
''
'Y  SAGE, AND Z, ITS STRICT FORM. EACH TAKES A FUNCTION AND GIVES'
'   BACK ITS FIXED POINT: RECURSION WITHOUT A NAME. APL\360 CANNOT'
'   GIVE ONE FUNCTION TO ANOTHER, NOR GIVE ONE BACK, SO NEITHER CAN'
'   BE WRITTEN. NOR IS EITHER NEEDED: A FUNCTION CALLS ITSELF BY'
'   NAME. FACT DOES, AND FACT 6 IS 720.'
''
'KI IS SMULLYAN''S K I, K GIVEN THE IDIOT. K CANNOT BE GIVEN A'
'   FUNCTION HERE, SO KI IS WRITTEN OUT INSTEAD.'
''
'AND T, B, C, W AND S REACH ONLY THE PRIMITIVES IN THE TABLES OF'
'APPLY AND DYAD. A DEFINED FUNCTION CANNOT BE NAMED TO THEM:'
'APL\360 HAS NO EXECUTE, SO A NAME IS ONLY CHARACTERS.'
∇
∇R←FG S X;FN
FN←FG[1]
R←X DYAD FG[2] APPLY X
∇
∇R←X T F
R←F APPLY X
∇
∇R←F W X;FN
FN←F
R←X DYAD X
∇
